                   <string>&lt;html&gt;&lt;head/&gt;&lt;body&gt;&lt;p&gt;Higher value can produce less detail in areas close to the camera.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/body&gt;&lt;/html&gt;</string>
                  </property>
                 </widget>
                </item>
                <item row="3" column="1">
                 <widget class="MyLineEdit" name="logedit_rel_min_marching_step">
                  <property name="toolTip">
                   <string>&lt;html&gt;&lt;head/&gt;&lt;body&gt;&lt;p&gt;Minimum relative step for raymarching. It is related to local detail size. Close to the camera, the limit is lower (visible details are smaller).&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Higher value can speed up calculation of raymarching in areas close to the fractal surface.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/body&gt;&lt;/html&gt;</string>
                  </property>
